{#
  vtysh's own configuration file.

  Without it vtysh falls back to reading frr.conf as its own config on EVERY
  invocation, fails the lines that are daemon configuration rather than vtysh
  configuration, and prints

    % Can't open configuration file /etc/frr/vtysh.conf ...
    Configuration file[/etc/frr/frr.conf] processing failure: 11

  ahead of the output of whatever you actually asked for. Nothing is wrong
  when that appears, which is precisely the problem: it looks like a fault,
  it is printed on healthy and broken labs alike, and it makes the real state
  harder to read at exactly the moment someone is debugging.
#}
service integrated-vtysh-config
